# .worktreeinclude — files copied into each new `claude -w` / isolation:worktree checkout.
# Syntax = .gitignore. Only files that match a pattern AND are gitignored get copied;
# tracked files are already checked out, so they never need listing.
#
# NOTE (verified 2026-07-01): a fresh worktree of this repo needs NOTHING copied to build/run —
#   - env.amarel.sh / env.ilab.sh ....... tracked (present in every checkout)
#   - external/nlohmann_json/json.hpp ... tracked (force-added past the external/ ignore)
#   - MuJoCo (MJ_PATH) .................. lives outside the repo, resolved from the env
# This file exists mainly as a forward-looking safety net for gitignored per-checkout config.

# --- per-checkout config: absent today, but if you ever create one it should follow every worktree ---
CLAUDE.local.md
.env
.env.local

# --- deliberately NOT copied ---
# external/h-levin/  : 22M, untracked, not referenced by this build (grep-verified).
# build_python/      : build artifact. A worktree should rebuild (./build_python_bindings.sh) so the
#                      compiled namo_rl matches ITS OWN C++. Copying the whole dir also drags a
#                      CMakeCache full of absolute source paths -> broken incremental builds.
#                      Python-only worktree and want to skip the rebuild? Uncomment to copy just the
#                      compiled module (safe; not the stale cmake dir):
# build_python/*.so
